# Unit tests stay in sync

When app behavior or code changes, update the matching tests in `app/src/test/` in the same work:

- Change or add tests so they describe the **new** behavior, not the old one.
- Prefer existing files (`V1WorkoutFlowTest`, `V1UiFlowTest`, `RestTimerStateTest`) unless a new area needs its own small test class.
- If a test is obsolete, delete or rewrite it — do not leave failing or lying tests.
- After test edits, run the relevant unit tests when a Gradle/JDK setup is available.
- Keep tests simple: one clear scenario, no extra frameworks unless already in the project.
